[Chapter "Sidelines"]
[Line "Accelerated Panov (2.c4)"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defense: Accelerated Panov Attack, Modern Variation"]

{White plays c4 before d4. Black regains the pawn with easy development.} 1. e4 c6 {The Caro-Kann.} 2. c4 d5 {Challenge the centre anyway.} 3. exd5 cxd5 {Recapture.} 4. cxd5 Nf6 {Don't take back with the queen: the knight wins the pawn back next move, with development.} 5. Nc3 Nxd5 {Pawn regained.} 6. Nf3 Nc6 {Natural development; Black has easy play.} *
